Part 1: Conjecture 3.2 on pair-lattice segments of spacing 2 (W = 2 at x = 0, 2, ..., 2(n-1)), v = 0.5
  LHS = sum_c Psi_c(sup_c Phi^-/2), RHS = E_P + pair r-bonds + sum W(W-2) (= 0 here).  Grid h = 1e-3, window +-60;
  rho_c = grid minimum of r on [0, d_c] (>= true minimum), grid sup of Phi^- (<= true sup), tail cells omitted:
  every approximation makes the LHS SMALLER.
  n =  8: E_P =  105.4925, bonds = 0.00273 | H1 cells l=0.5:  109.9597 (ratio 1.0423), l=0.6: 1.0053, l=0.7: 0.9636, best l: ratio 0.9636 | optimal cells:  101.3749 (ratio 0.9609)
  n = 20: E_P =  237.6547, bonds = 0.00924 | H1 cells l=0.5:  265.3726 (ratio 1.1166), l=0.6: 1.0983, l=0.7: 1.0797, best l: ratio 1.0797 | optimal cells:  255.2447 (ratio 1.0740)
  n = 40: E_P =  453.1229, bonds = 0.02241 | H1 cells l=0.5:  524.0374 (ratio 1.1564), l=0.6: 1.1491, l=0.7: 1.1394, best l: ratio 1.1394 | optimal cells:  513.2145 (ratio 1.1326)
