Part 5: field-energy duality at one point.  Lemma 5.1 of the memo (PROVED): Phi_Q(y)^2 <= tau_0(v) E_P, tau_0 = int rho tanh^2(pi a v),
  sharp over signed P.  Positive P (NUMERICAL, convex QP over densities nu >= 0 on [-6, 6], mesh 0.1; window-limited, so lower bounds):
  kappa_+(v) = sup Phi_Q^-(0)^2 / E_P ;  kappa(v) = sup Phi^-(0)^2 / (E_P + pair r-bonds)  (continuum limit, integrality irrelevant at scale)
  v = 0.2: tau_0 = 0.0536 | kappa_+ >= 0.0502 | kappa >= 0.0033 | one pair alone: max Q_v^-(t)^2/X(v) = 0.0181
  v = 0.5: tau_0 = 0.2360 | kappa_+ >= 0.2227 | kappa >= 0.1109 | one pair alone: max Q_v^-(t)^2/X(v) = 0.0731
  v = 1.0: tau_0 = 0.4861 | kappa_+ >= 0.4595 | kappa >= 0.3809 | one pair alone: max Q_v^-(t)^2/X(v) = 0.0852
  v = 2.0: tau_0 = 0.7128 | kappa_+ >= 0.6594 | kappa >= 0.6345 | one pair alone: max Q_v^-(t)^2/X(v) = 0.0325
  Lemma 5.1 check on random signed configurations: max (sum b Phi_Q)^2 / (E_P b'Mb) = 0.639203 (<= 1)   [337s]

Part 6: continuum one-layer configurations: pairs with density Lambda*nu, nu = beta - b >= 0, one real atom of weight Lambda at 0,
  b = FT^{-1}[sech(2 pi a v)] = sech(pi x/(2v))/(2v), beta = sech(pi theta x/(2v))/(2v) (theta < 1).  Then S_Z/Lambda = c * beta^ exactly, and
  [Sigma_Z(rho) - int shat |S_Z0|^2]/Lambda^2 = Q = int rho c^2 |beta^|^2 - int shat |1 + nu^|^2   (order Lambda^2; costs are O(Lambda))
  int shat = 0.012460  (= s(0) = R - 1)
  v =  10, theta = 1/2: int rho c^2 |beta^|^2 = 0.08211, s-hat term = 0.01246, Q = +0.06965
  v =  20, theta = 1/2: int rho c^2 |beta^|^2 = 0.04108, s-hat term = 0.01246, Q = +0.02862
  v =  50, theta = 1/2: int rho c^2 |beta^|^2 = 0.01644, s-hat term = 0.01246, Q = +0.00398
  v =  66, theta = 1/2: int rho c^2 |beta^|^2 = 0.01245, s-hat term = 0.01246, Q = -0.00001
  v =  70, theta = 1/2: int rho c^2 |beta^|^2 = 0.01174, s-hat term = 0.01246, Q = -0.00072
  v = 100, theta = 1/2: int rho c^2 |beta^|^2 = 0.00822, s-hat term = 0.01246, Q = -0.00424
  v = 200, theta = 1/2: int rho c^2 |beta^|^2 = 0.00411, s-hat term = 0.01246, Q = -0.00835
  -> Q < 0 for v >~ 66: dropping int shat|S_Z0|^2 (H1-type reductions, 3.2, 3.2') loses (**) at order Lambda^2 there (HEURISTIC transfer)   [338s]

